  "result": "```json\n{\n    \"smpl.ordering.models.ShipmentRecord\": {\n        \"summary\": \"Represents data for a particular shipment in an ordering system. Each order corresponds to no more than one shipment record, meaning shipments are consolidated. The orderId serves as the key identifier for the shipment record, establishing a one-to-one relationship with orders. Key methods include: standard getters/setters for all properties (orderId, deliveryDate, deliveryAddress, contactName, primaryContactPhone, alternateContactPhone); addEvent() methods to track shipment events with date and comments; a default constructor that initializes an empty events list; a copy constructor that performs deep copying of all fields including events; and validate() which checks that required fields (orderId, deliveryDate, deliveryAddress, contactName, primaryContactPhone) are present and returns null if valid or error messages if validation fails. The class maintains a final list of ShipmentEventInfo objects to track shipment history and uses related model classes like DeliveryAddress and PhoneInfo for structured data.\",\n        \"file_path\": \"smpl/ordering/models/ShipmentRecord.java\"\n    }\n}\n```",
